<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    FSD Gap Closure Tranche 2, Item 3 (§24.1) - 2026-08-16.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit
    go-ahead. This file only DESCRIBES a deletion; it performs nothing on its own.

    Retires Deal_Tracker_LOI and Deal_Tracker_PSA (both Opportunity ListViews),
    superseded by the five-way split delivered in this same tranche:
    Deal_Tracker_LOI_Pending, Deal_Tracker_LOI_Submitted, Deal_Tracker_LOI_Accepted,
    Deal_Tracker_PSA_Negotiation, Deal_Tracker_PSA_Executed - all filtered on the
    new Opportunity.Deal_Sub_Stage__c formula field. Leaving the two originals in
    place alongside the five splits would produce TEN "Deal Tracker" views where
    the FSD names eight.

    POST-destructive gate G8 (design-requirements-fsd-tranche-2.md): before this
    deploys, verify neither retired view is pinned in anyone's Lightning nav or
    referenced by an org-side report - list-view references from those surfaces
    are not represented in this repo and this manifest cannot detect them.

    Deploy (only once authorised by the user, and only after G2 confirms
    Deal_Sub_Stage__c is filterable in the org - see the field's own XML comment):
      sf project deploy start \
        --manifest manifest/deal-tracker-loi-psa-retire/package.xml \
        --post-destructive-changes manifest/deal-tracker-loi-psa-retire/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
        --target-org usman-dpeg \
        --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

    Rollback: a deleted ListView is recoverable from git history (this repo held
    both files up to this same commit) and can be re-created by a fresh deploy.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>Opportunity.Deal_Tracker_LOI</members>
        <members>Opportunity.Deal_Tracker_PSA</members>
        <name>ListView</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
